### TextProcessing/MarkdownStripper.cs

| # | Severity | Finding |
|---|----------|---------|
| 1 | 🟡 Moderate | **46 `RegexOptions.Compiled` instances** — Each compiled regex JIT-compiles at first use, adding ~200ms+ of startup time collectively. On .NET 8+, `[GeneratedRegex]` source-generates IL at build time with zero startup cost. |
| 2 | ℹ️ Info | **Long chain of `.Replace()` calls in `StripMarkdown`** — 46 sequential string allocations. For very large documents this is significant, but each individual regex must run sequentially anyway. Consider a single-pass approach or at minimum batch related patterns. |
